; Russian Cards Problem, classic 3-3-1 deal over seven cards.
; Alice publicly announces a Fano plane containing her hand as a line.
; Bob identifies the unique line disjoint from his hand; Eve's card leaves
; four possible Alice lines, so she cannot identify any one of Alice's cards.
; The random role deals uniformly over the 140 deals; Alice chooses among
; the six Fano planes containing her hand.
;@instructions THE RUSSIAN CARDS PROBLEM
;@instructions Seven cards are dealt: Alice and Bob each receive three, and Eve receives the remaining card.
;@instructions Alice publicly announces one of seven Fano planes containing her hand. Each plane is a collection of seven three-card lines.
;@instructions After the announcement, Bob should be able to identify Alice's exact hand, while Eve should still be unable to identify any one of Alice's cards.
;@instructions Alice chooses the announcement. The other players' knowledge can be inspected with :q bob aliceHand(A,B,C) and :q eve aliceHand(A,B,C).


